<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conquest of the Desert</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Conquest of the Desert was the Argentine military campaign, led by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julio-argentino-roca">Julio Argentino Roca</a> from 1878 to 1879 and continued until 1885, that seized the pampas and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patagonia">Patagonia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehuelche">Tehuelche</a> and other indigenous peoples. Thousands were killed or displaced, the Salinas Grandes confederation was destroyed, and the land opened to settlement and large estates.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conquest-of-the-desert.jpg" alt="Conquest of the Desert" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Manuel Blanes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_conquista_del_desierto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
